  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/wbjee/2013_che_a13.png\">\r\n\r\n$\\begin{array}{ll}\\text {Hydrozine, } & \\mathrm{NH}_{2} \\cdot \\mathrm{NH}_{2} \\text { does not respond }\\end{array}$\r\nLassaigne's test because it does not contain any carbon and hence, NaCN is not formed. Compound, $\\mathrm{NH}_{2}-\\mathrm{CS}-\\mathrm{NH}_{2}$ contains both $\\mathrm{N}$ and $\\mathrm{S}$, hence, it will give red colour in Lassaigne test.",
